- crates/catbot-ui/tailwind.css is adapted from OpenMausBot's src/styles.css
  (colour tokens, skins, spacing, type). Changes: font imports replaced; Tailwind
  scans Catbot's sources.
- The interface reproduces OpenMausBot's layout and Tailwind class names.
- Catbot's server speaks OpenMausBot's wire protocol.
- How Catbot's bot pictures move (crates/catbot-ui/assets/mascots.css and the page
  script in crates/catbot-ui/src/mascots.rs) is adapted from OpenMausBot's
  src/components/mascot-motion.ts, CursorAvatar.tsx and Avatar.tsx: the per-state
  body motions, blink cadence and pointer gaze, rewritten as CSS animations and a
  small script. The pictures themselves are Catbot's own.
- jsQR 1.4.0 (crates/catbot-ui/assets/jsQR.js), by Cosmo Wolfe, Apache-2.0
  (third_party/jsQR-LICENSE): the phone app reads pairing QR codes with it
  when the phone's browser engine has no BarcodeDetector of its own.
- How Catbot runs bots on chat APIs and agent programs (crates/catbot/src/engines.rs,
  api.rs, acp.rs) follows OpenMausBot's server/drivers/ (the built-in driver list, their
  addresses, flags and sign-in commands, openai-chat.ts and acp/core.ts in outline).
- How Catbot names chats (crates/catbot/src/titles.rs) is adapted from
  OpenMausBot's server/thread-title.ts and thread-title-generate.ts: the
  first-line name, the naming prompt and how the reply is cleaned.
- Moving a Grok Bot (crates/catbot/src/server/grok_move.rs) follows OpenMausBot's
  shared/grok-import.ts and server/grok-local.ts: the export's JSON shape and the
  prompt that asks for it (reworded), the repairs for what a chat window does to
  it, merging split exports, refusing credential-looking fields, and finding
  exports in Downloads. Rewritten in Rust; Catbot makes bots, skills, triggers
  and memory notes of its own from it.
- Continue with ChatGPT (crates/catbot/src/chatgpt.rs) follows OpenMausBot's
  server/drivers/chatgpt-plan-auth.ts and codex-plan-token.ts: the agent sign-in
  at auth.openai.com (its parameters, scopes and checks), keeping and renewing
  the tokens, and the Codex settings that point a turn at the plan. Rewritten
  in Rust.

